{title: 686 - Bless Thou the Gifts}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #686 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 686}
{meta: category Sentences and Responses - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D7]Bless [G]Thou [B7]the [Em]gifts [Am7]our [D7]hands [C]have [G]brought;
[G]Bless [C]Thou [D7]the [G]work [A]our [D]hearts [A7]have [D]planned.
[D7]Ours [G]is [B]the [E]faith, [Am7]the [D7]will, [C]the [G]thought;
[G]The [C]rest, [D7]O[Em]God, [A7]is [G]in [D]Thy [G]hand.
[C]A[G]men.
{end_of_verse}
